<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Sacred · date unknown · Ancient Near East</p><h1 class="sg-title">Psalm 104</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תהילים קד</bdi> / <bdi lang="hbo-Latn">Tehillim 104</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>An ancient Hebrew hymn that praises God as the maker of the world, from the sky and the seas to the animals, plants and people.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>anonymous</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>ancient Israelites; Jewish and Christian worshippers</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Biblical Hebrew</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>not known; the article sets the Great Hymn to the Aten (14th century BCE) some 400 years before it</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Sacred</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (words anonymous (Book of Psalms, Hebrew Bible))</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psalm-104">Psalm 104</a> is the 104th psalm of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-psalms">Book of Psalms</a>; in the slightly different numbering of the Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septuagint">Septuagint</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Vulgate it is Psalm 103, known in Latin as &quot;Benedic anima mea Domino&quot;. One of the longer psalms, it is traditionally divided into 35 verses. It is the first place in the Old Testament where the word &quot;Hallelujah&quot; occurs, followed by Psalms 105 and 106, which O. Palmer Robertson sees with it as a triad closing the fourth book of the Psalms. In the Masoretic text the Hallelujah stands at the end of its last verse and is read as the opening of the next psalm; the Septuagint and the Vulgate lack it.</p><p>The psalm is a hymn of creation whose order follows the creation story of Genesis 1. Commentators find in it a chiastic structure: it opens and closes with praise of God's royal splendour, and between them come the forming of the earth, the waters and the animals, the regular round of the moon and the sun, the sea with its creatures, and the dependence of every creature on God's continuing care. It makes clear that even &quot;the deep&quot; was created by God and did not exist before him, as in Babylonian creation myth, and it names the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leviathan">Leviathan</a> as just another of God's creatures rather than a rival to his authority, as surrounding Canaanite peoples believed. Its last verse wishes that sinners and the wicked be consumed out of the earth.</p><p>The psalm bears a notable resemblance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhenaten">Akhenaten</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-hymn-to-the-aten">Great Hymn to the Aten</a>, written some 400 years earlier in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and it is often cited as a parallel text. Commentators note that in the biblical text the sun and the rest of creation are not gods but creations, so that the psalm is &quot;implicitly antipagan&quot; and seems to comment on such hymns rather than copy them. Mark S. Smith observes that enthusiasm for even indirect influence has cooled in recent decades and that some reject it outright, while Egyptologists such as Jan Assmann and Donald Redford still argue for Egyptian influence.</p><p>The psalm has a regular place in Jewish, Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a>, Catholic, Lutheran, Anglican and other Protestant worship. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-testament">New Testament</a> quotes its fourth verse in the Letter to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrews</a>. Many observant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> recite it in the morning service of the New Moon (Rosh Chodesh), and many communities after the Sabbath afternoon service between Sukkot and Shabbat Hagadol; single verses stand in the daily prayers. In the Eastern Orthodox Church it opens Vespers every day, read by the senior reader, or sung by the choir with refrains at the All-Night Vigil on feast days; there it is often taken as Adam's song outside the closed gates of Eden, while the priest stands before the closed Royal Doors. The Catholic Church sings it as the responsorial psalm after the creation reading of the Easter Vigil, and again at Pentecost; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-common-prayer">Book of Common Prayer</a> appoints it for the evening of the twentieth day of the month and for Evensong on Whitsunday. The theologian Jaime Pérez de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> (1408–1490) read its ninth verse as confirming Ptolemy's view that the oceans were surrounded by land, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-gottfried-herder">Johann Gottfried Herder</a> remarked that it was worth studying Hebrew for ten years to read it in the original.</p><p>It has often been set to music. John Dowland's English setting appeared in Thomas Est's Whole Booke of Psalmes of 1592, Heinrich Schütz set a metrical German text for the Becker <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-psalms">Psalter</a> of 1628, and Bach set two of its verses in his cantata Es wartet alles auf dich (1726). Sir Robert Grant's hymn &quot;O Worship the King&quot;, first published in 1833, is based on it, and Philip <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gla">Glass</a> set it in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> in his opera Akhnaten. Prince Philip, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>, commissioned a setting from William Lovelady for his 75th birthday; an abridged version for four-part choir and organ was sung at his funeral in St George's Chapel, Windsor, on 17 April 2021.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A hymn that praises God as a king robed in light who made and keeps the world: he set the earth on its foundations and bounded the waters, sends springs and rain for the wild animals, the birds, the herds and the crops of people, made the moon and sun to mark the times of night and day, and filled the sea with creatures. Every living thing waits on him and lives by his breath. The mood is one of wonder and joyful praise, closing in a vow to sing to God for life.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-blocks sg-blocks-2"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-1"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">Biblical Hebrew</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">בָּרְﬞכִ֥י נַפְשִׁ֗י אֶת־יְ֫הֹוָ֥ה</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יְהֹוָ֣ה אֱ֭לֹהַי גָּדַ֣לְתָּ מְּאֹ֑ד</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">ה֖וֹד וְהָדָ֣ר לָבָֽשְׁתָּ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">עֹֽטֶה־א֭וֹר כַּשַּׂלְמָ֑ה</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">נוֹטֶ֥ה שָׁ֝מַ֗יִם כַּיְרִיעָֽה׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הַ֥מְﬞקָרֶ֥ה בַמַּ֗יִם עֲֽלִיּ֫וֹתָ֥יו</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הַשָּׂם־עָבִ֥ים רְכוּב֑וֹ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הַֽ֝מְﬞהַלֵּ֗ךְ עַל־כַּנְפֵי־רֽוּחַ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">עֹשֶׂ֣ה מַלְאָכָ֣יו רוּח֑וֹת</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מְ֝שָׁרְתָ֗יו אֵ֣שׁ לֹהֵֽט׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יָֽסַד־אֶ֭רֶץ עַל־מְכוֹנֶ֑יהָ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">בַּל־תִּ֝מּ֗וֹט עוֹלָ֥ם וָעֶֽד׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תְּ֭הוֹם כַּלְּב֣וּשׁ כִּסִּית֑וֹ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">עַל־הָ֝רִ֗ים יַ֖עַמְדוּ־מָֽיִם׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מִן־גַּעֲרָ֣תְךָ֣ יְנוּס֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מִן־ק֥וֹל רַ֝עַמְךָ֗ יֵחָפֵזֽוּן׃</span></p></div><details class="sg-more"><summary>Show all 79 lines</summary><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יַעֲל֣וּ הָ֭רִים יֵרְד֣וּ בְקָע֑וֹת</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">אֶל־מְ֝ק֗וֹם זֶ֤ה ׀ יָסַ֬דְתָּ לָהֶֽם׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">גְּֽבוּל־שַׂ֭מְתָּ בַּל־יַעֲבֹר֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">בַּל־יְ֝שֻׁב֗וּן לְכַסּ֥וֹת הָאָֽרֶץ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הַֽמְﬞשַׁלֵּ֣חַ מַ֭עְיָנִים בַּנְּחָלִ֑ים</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">בֵּ֥ין הָ֝רִ֗ים יְהַלֵּכֽוּן׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יַ֭שְׁקוּ כׇּל־חַיְת֣וֹ שָׂדָ֑י</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יִשְׁבְּר֖וּ פְרָאִ֣ים צְמָאָֽם׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">עֲ֭לֵיהֶם עוֹף־הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם יִשְׁכּ֑וֹן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מִבֵּ֥ין עֳ֝פָאיִ֗ם יִתְּנוּ־קֽוֹל׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מַשְׁקֶ֣ה הָ֭רִים מֵעֲלִיּוֹתָ֑יו</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מִפְּרִ֥י מַ֝עֲשֶׂ֗יךָ תִּשְׂבַּ֥ע הָאָֽרֶץ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מַצְמִ֤יחַ חָצִ֨יר ׀ לַבְּהֵמָ֗ה</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וְ֭עֵשֶׂב לַעֲבֹדַ֣ת הָאָדָ֑ם</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">לְה֥וֹצִיא לֶ֗֝חֶם מִן־הָאָֽרֶץ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וְיַ֤יִן ׀ יְשַׂמַּ֬ח לְֽבַב־אֱנ֗וֹשׁ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">לְהַצְהִ֣יל פָּנִ֣ים מִשָּׁ֑מֶן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וְ֝לֶ֗חֶם לְֽבַב־אֱנ֥וֹשׁ יִסְעָֽד׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יִ֭שְׂבְּעוּ עֲצֵ֣י יְהֹוָ֑ה</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">אַֽרְזֵ֥י לְ֝בָנ֗וֹן אֲשֶׁ֣ר נָטָֽע׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">אֲשֶׁר־שָׁ֭ם צִפֳּרִ֣ים יְקַנֵּ֑נוּ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">חֲ֝סִידָ֗ה בְּרוֹשִׁ֥ים בֵּיתָֽהּ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הָרִ֣ים הַ֭גְּבֹהִים לַיְּעֵלִ֑ים</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">סְ֝לָעִ֗ים מַחְסֶ֥ה לַֽשְׁﬞפַנִּֽים׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">עָשָׂ֣ה יָ֭רֵחַ לְמוֹעֲדִ֑ים</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">שֶׁ֝֗מֶשׁ יָדַ֥ע מְבוֹאֽוֹ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תָּֽשֶׁת־חֹ֭שֶׁךְ וִ֣יהִי לָ֑יְלָה</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">בּוֹ־תִ֝רְמֹ֗שׂ כׇּל־חַיְתוֹ־יָֽעַר׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הַ֭כְּפִירִים שֹׁאֲגִ֣ים לַטָּ֑רֶף</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וּלְבַקֵּ֖שׁ מֵאֵ֣ל אׇכְלָֽם׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תִּזְרַ֣ח הַ֭שֶּׁמֶשׁ יֵאָסֵפ֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וְאֶל־מְ֝עוֹנֹתָ֗ם יִרְבָּצֽוּן׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יֵצֵ֣א אָדָ֣ם לְפׇעֳל֑וֹ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וְֽלַעֲבֹ֖דָת֣וֹ עֲדֵי־עָֽרֶב׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מָה־רַבּ֬וּ מַעֲשֶׂ֨יךָ ׀ יְֽהֹוָ֗ה</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">כֻּ֭לָּם בְּחׇכְמָ֣ה עָשִׂ֑יתָ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">מָלְאָ֥ה הָ֝אָ֗רֶץ קִנְיָנֶֽךָ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">זֶ֤ה ׀ הַיָּ֥ם גָּדוֹל֮ וּרְחַ֢ב יָ֫דָ֥יִם</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">שָֽׁם־רֶ֭מֶשׂ וְאֵ֣ין מִסְפָּ֑ר</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">חַיּ֥וֹת קְ֝טַנּ֗וֹת עִם־גְּדֹלֽוֹת׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">שָׁ֭ם אֳנִיּ֣וֹת יְהַלֵּכ֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">לִ֝וְיָתָ֗ן זֶֽה־יָצַ֥רְתָּ לְשַֽׂחֶק־בּֽוֹ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">כֻּ֭לָּם אֵלֶ֣יךָ יְשַׂבֵּר֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">לָתֵ֖ת אׇכְלָ֣ם בְּעִתּֽוֹ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תִּתֵּ֣ן לָ֭הֶם יִלְקֹט֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תִּפְתַּ֥ח יָ֝דְךָ֗ יִשְׂבְּע֥וּן טֽוֹב׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תַּסְתִּ֥יר פָּנֶ֮יךָ֮ יִֽבָּהֵ֫ל֥וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תֹּסֵ֣ף ר֭וּחָם יִגְוָע֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וְֽאֶל־עֲפָרָ֥ם יְשׁוּבֽוּן׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">תְּשַׁלַּ֣ח ר֭וּחֲךָ יִבָּרֵא֑וּן</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וּ֝תְחַדֵּ֗שׁ פְּנֵ֣י אֲדָמָֽה׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יְהִ֤י כְב֣וֹד יְהֹוָ֣ה לְעוֹלָ֑ם</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יִשְׂמַ֖ח יְהֹוָ֣ה בְּמַעֲשָֽׂיו׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הַמַּבִּ֣יט לָ֭אָרֶץ וַתִּרְעָ֑ד</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יִגַּ֖ע בֶּהָרִ֣ים וְֽיֶעֱשָֽׁנוּ׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">אָשִׁ֣ירָה לַיהֹוָ֣ה בְּחַיָּ֑י</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">אֲזַמְּרָ֖ה לֵאלֹהַ֣י בְּעוֹדִֽי׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יֶעֱרַ֣ב עָלָ֣יו שִׂיחִ֑י</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">אָ֝נֹכִ֗י אֶשְׂמַ֥ח בַּיהֹוָֽה׃</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">יִתַּ֤מּוּ חַטָּאִ֨ים ׀ מִן־הָאָ֡רֶץ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">וּרְשָׁעִ֤ים ׀ ע֤וֹד אֵינָ֗ם</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">בָּרְﬞכִ֣י נַ֭פְשִׁי אֶת־יְהֹוָ֗ה</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="hbo" dir="rtl">הַֽלְﬞלוּ־יָֽהּ׃</span></p></div></details></div><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-1"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-e">In English</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Bless the LORD, O my soul. O LORD my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honour and majesty.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Who coverest thyself with light as with a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters: who maketh the clouds his chariot: who walketh upon the wings of the wind:</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Who laid the foundations of the earth, that it should not be removed for ever.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thou coveredst it with the deep as with a garment: the waters stood above the mountains.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>They go up by the mountains; they go down by the valleys unto the place which thou hast founded for them.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>He sendeth the springs into the valleys, which run among the hills.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>They give drink to every beast of the field: the wild asses quench their thirst.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>By them shall the fowls of the heaven have their habitation, which sing among the branches.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>He watereth the hills from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>And wine that maketh glad the heart of man, and oil to make his face to shine, and bread which strengtheneth man's heart.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>The trees of the LORD are full of sap; the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Where the birds make their nests: as for the stork, the fir trees are her house.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>The high hills are a refuge for the wild goats; and the rocks for the conies.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thou makest darkness, and it is night: wherein all the beasts of the forest do creep forth.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their meat from God.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>The sun ariseth, they gather themselves together, and lay them down in their dens.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Man goeth forth unto his work and to his labour until the evening.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>O LORD, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>So is this great and wide sea, wherein are things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>There go the ships: there is that leviathan, whom thou hast made to play therein.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give them their meat in due season.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>That thou givest them they gather: thou openest thine hand, they are filled with good.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled: thou takest away their breath, they die, and return to their dust.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created: and thou renewest the face of the earth.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>The glory of the LORD shall endure for ever: the LORD shall rejoice in his works.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>He looketh on the earth, and it trembleth: he toucheth the hills, and they smoke.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>I will sing unto the LORD as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>My meditation of him shall be sweet: I will be glad in the LORD.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-e" data-say>Let the sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless thou the LORD, O my soul. Praise ye the LORD.</span></p></div></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: Psalm 104, Hebrew Bible (Masoretic text). Text from <a href="https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%AA%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%99%D7%9D_%D7%A7%D7%93" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p><p>English: King James Version (1611). Text from <a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Bible_(King_James)%2FPsalms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p></div></section>
